        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Calculate the period of the sine function.\nThe period of the sine function is the distance between two consecutive peaks or troughs. From the graph, the period appears to be $\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$. The period of a sine function $y = a \\sin(bx + c) + d$ is given by $\\frac{2\\pi}{b}$. Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{2\\pi}{b} = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} \\implies b = 3\n\\]"
      },
